    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. While that's a strong take, some economists argue that UBI is fiscally irresponsible and could actually trigger massive inflation or devalue the currency, which would destabilize the very society we're trying to protect. They also claim that targeted programs are much more efficient because they direct resources to those who actually need them most, rather than giving money to people who don't. How would you respond to the argument that UBI is essentially a massive, inefficient waste of capital compared to targeted support?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
